codex
Both in-scope P1 fixes pass source inspection. The half-open retirement interval covers the first request and isolates descendants correctly; the persisted drain advances through irrelevant answers and recovers from gaps without spending `:checks`.

The rollback, verification-cost, and executable AD-0 requirements are also present. I found three non-blocking clarifications: answer-ID comparison wording, the acceptance test’s expected retired set, and the claim about when answer-ring eviction can occur.
